# core.autocrlf is true on this machine, and git was classifying the
# generated PDFs as text: committing one printed "LF will be replaced by
# CRLF the next time Git touches it". Today's files survive that only
# because they happen to contain no CRLF sequences -- a fresh clone of a
# less lucky build would check out a corrupted download. Mark them binary
# so no line-ending filter ever runs over them.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
